    </property>
    <property name="toolTip">
     <string>Centre audio frequency (Hz) for channel A. Standard VHF packet uses 1700 (between Bell-202 1200/2200 Hz tones).</string>
    </property>
    <property name="whatsThis">
     <string>&lt;b&gt;Channel A centre frequency (Hz)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The audio centre of the demodulator passband. Standard VHF packet practice is &lt;tt&gt;1700&lt;/tt&gt; Hz, sitting symmetrically between the Bell-202 mark (1200 Hz) and space (2200 Hz) tones. HF and other modes may pick different centres. Range 0–3000 Hz; default 1700.&lt;br/&gt;Stored as &lt;tt&gt;Modem/RXFreq1&lt;/tt&gt;.</string>
    </property>
   </widget>
   <widget class="QComboBox" name="modeB">
    <property name="geometry">
     <rect>
      <x>316</x>
      <y>6</y>
      <width>145</width>
      <height>22</height>
     </rect>
    </property>
    <property name="toolTip">
     <string>Modem mode for channel B — selects the modulator/demodulator (AFSK 1200, G3RUH 9600, BPSK 300, etc.).</string>
    </property>
    <property name="whatsThis">
     <string>&lt;b&gt;Channel B modem mode&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;Sets the modulator and demodulator used on this channel. Match it to the on-air signal — common choices are AFSK 1200 for VHF packet, G3RUH 9600 for 9600-baud packet, BPSK 300 for HF packet, and V.26/V.27 for higher-rate HF. Open the dropdown for the full list, or see Help → User Guide for descriptions of each. IL2P framing is configured separately in Setup Modems.&lt;br/&gt;Stored as &lt;tt&gt;Modem/ModemType2&lt;/tt&gt;.</string>
    </property>
   </widget>
